    {
      "title": "Undercover report on donations ‘looks bad’ for Reform, admits Nigel Farage – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/06/nigel-farage-reform-uk-donations-undercover-investigation-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>The Reform UK leader is under pressure after senior aides appeared to plot how to bypass electoral laws on foreign donations</p><p>Sagal Abdi-Wali arrived in Camden as a child refugee from Somalia. She has worked for more than a decade as a volunteer and trustee for local charities and is a governor of two schools in the borough, according to Labour.</p><p>She was first elected as a councillor in 2022 and became the leader of the council in May, when she said: “Camden has been my home for 35 years. It is the place that gave my family sanctuary, that welcomed us, and that has shaped so much of who I am, what I stand for and what inspired my commitment to public service and to working for the community that welcomed us.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/06/nigel-farage-reform-uk-donations-undercover-investigation-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T12:50:58"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zia Yusuf’s post about Camden council leader is ‘straightforward racism’, says minister",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/06/zia-yusuf-reform-uk-post-camden-council-leader-sagal-abdi-wali",
      "description": "<p>Senior Reform UK figure has faced criticism within party after post about Sagal Abdi-Wali, a former child refugee</p><p>Labour has accused Reform’s Zia Yusuf of “straightforward racism” after he suggested the party’s frontrunner to replace Keir Starmer in the Holborn and St Pancras byelection was not British.</p><p>Sagal Abdi-Wali, a former child refugee from Somalia and the leader of Camden council, has been tipped as an early favourite to contest the London seat for Labour after the former prime minister’s resignation.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/06/zia-yusuf-reform-uk-post-camden-council-leader-sagal-abdi-wali\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T12:15:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Farage says overseas donation row ‘looks bad’ but denies Reform broke law",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/06/farage-says-overseas-donation-row-looks-bad-but-denies-reform-breached-electoral-law",
      "description": "<p>Robert Jenrick says party has followed legal protocol ‘at all times’ as Met police consider launching investigation</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/06/nigel-farage-reform-uk-donations-undercover-investigation-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Nigel Farage has acknowledged the overseas donation row engulfing Reform UK “looks bad” for his party but denied it had ever taken foreign money in breach of electoral law.</p><p>The Reform leader, who is battling to contain the fallout from the allegations, was asked if he could categorically rule out that foreign money had ever been funnelled to his party. He replied: “I can. Never happened.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/06/farage-says-overseas-donation-row-looks-bad-but-denies-reform-breached-electoral-law\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-06T11:12:09"
    },
